    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461-a1">

                <pb facs="0556" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg468"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have received your
                    excellency’s note, dated the 20th instant, in which further request is made for
                    the good offices of this department to expedite the judicial proceedings in the
                    case of H. C. Harding and H. E. Dugat, charged with infraction of the general
                    customs regulations.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say to your excellency that I have already addressed
                    the district judge who has charge of the matter asking him for a report upon the
                    case.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
